From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: athexweb3 <athexweb3@nirapod.org>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 19:44:12 +0600
Subject: [PATCH] safetylib: option to pass on congruences for written
 variables only

The reduced product of the numerical and congruence domains meets every
congruence fact into the numerical state after every operation. With
"congruence_reduction": 1, an operation that writes variables (assignment,
forgetting, repacking) passes on only the facts on those variables; other
operations pass on all of them. With 0, none is passed on; the congruence
domain is still used by the checks. The default, 2, keeps the current
behaviour. Passing a fact on only refines the numerical state, so lower
values can only add alarms.

Signed-off-by: athexweb3 <athexweb3@nirapod.org>
---
 compiler/safetylib/domains/safetyBoolean.ml   | 16 ++++++++
 compiler/safetylib/domains/safetyProduct.ml   | 38 +++++++++++++------
 compiler/safetylib/domains/safetyProduct.mli  |  4 ++
 compiler/safetylib/safetyConfig.ml            | 13 +++++++
 compiler/safetylib/safetyConfig.mli           |  1 +
 .../tests/safety/congruence.t/aligned.jazz    | 12 ++++++
 compiler/tests/safety/congruence.t/cr0.json   |  1 +
